---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="For Schools — The Technology Behind Mt Cedar"
  description="ResultPeak AI and JDSmartLearn: the assessment platform and lesson system built for Nigerian schools and used every day at Mt Cedar British International School. Request a walkthrough."
  active=""
>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">For Other Schools</p>
    <h1>The software we built, and use every day.</h1>
    <p>Two systems run the assessment and lesson side of Mt Cedar. They were written here, for the realities of a Nigerian school, and other schools are welcome to use them.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Why We Built Them</p><h2>Written for the school we actually run.</h2><p>Most school software assumes a computer per child, a reliable connection, and a parent with an email address. That is not the school day here.</p></div>
    <div class="feat-grid">
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><rect x="6" y="2" width="12" height="20" rx="2.5"/><path d="M11 18.5h2"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Built for the phone in the room</h3>
        <p>A mid-range Android on mobile data is the target device, not a laptop. Lessons stay readable once loaded, so a bundle running out does not end the school day.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg></div>
        <h3>No accounts to manage</h3>
        <p>Students sign in with a short username and an access code printed by the school. No email addresses for minors, no password resets, nothing for a parent to set up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M12 2 3 7v6c0 5 3.5 8 9 9 5.5-1 9-4 9-9V7l-9-5Z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>A teacher signs off everything</h3>
        <p>AI drafts and AI marking are a first pass, never the last word. No score reaches a result sheet and no lesson reaches a student without a teacher having reviewed it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">The Two Systems</p><h2>Assessment, and lessons.</h2></div>
    <div class="feat-grid two">
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M9 3h6a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1H8V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z"/><path d="M8 5H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v12a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-2"/><path d="m9 13 2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>ResultPeak AI</h3>
        <p>An assessment platform that takes each school on its own terms: your subjects, your assessment structure — mid-term test, project, examination — and your grading scale.</p>
        <p>Objective questions are marked on submission. Written answers are marked with AI assistance and queued for tutor review. Scores flow into your term result sheet, ready to print or download.</p>
        <p>Roles run superadmin, school administrator, tutor, student.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M12 7c-1.8-1.3-4-2-6.5-2H3v13h2.5c2.5 0 4.7.7 6.5 2 1.8-1.3 4-2 6.5-2H21V5h-2.5C16 5 13.8 5.7 12 7Z"/><path d="M12 7v13"/></svg></div>
        <h3>JDSmartLearn</h3>
        <p>A lesson system for primary and secondary. A tutor uploads a lesson; it comes back as a student summary, a set of practice questions, and a marking guide only the tutor can see.</p>
        <p>The tutor edits and publishes. Students read it on their phone, offline once it has loaded.</p>
        <p>It runs on the same roster as ResultPeak, so one username and code opens both.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Honest Scope</p><h2>What these do not do.</h2><p>Deliberately left out, so that what remains is solid. Some of it is planned; some of it is somebody else's product.</p></div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="lead-copy">
        <p><strong>Not built, and not planned for now:</strong> live classes, video lessons, attendance registers, timetabling, and native mobile apps. Each one is a product in its own right, and doing them badly would weaken the parts that work.</p>
        <p><strong>Under consideration for a later version:</strong> school fee payments, parent messaging, and video. They are real needs; they are not the first thing to get right.</p>
        <p>If one of those is the reason you are looking for software, we would rather tell you now than sell you a plan.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cform" style="align-self:start">
        <h3 style="font-family:var(--display);font-size:1.4rem;margin:0 0 .3rem">See it working</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 1.2rem;font-size:.98rem">A walkthrough with a school administrator takes about half an hour, and we will use your subjects and your grading scale rather than a demo dataset.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-cedar" style="width:100%;margin-bottom:.7rem" href="mailto:mtcedarbritishinternationalsch@gmail.com?subject=ResultPeak%20%2F%20JDSmartLearn%20enquiry%20%28from%20For%20Schools%20page%29">Request a Walkthrough</a>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:1rem 0 0;font-size:.88rem">This enquiry is about the software. For admissions to Mt Cedar, please use the <a href="/admissions" style="color:var(--cedar);font-weight:700">admissions page</a> instead.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold-bright)">Built in Benin City</p>
    <h2>Tested in a real school, every term.</h2>
    <p>Both systems are used by Mt Cedar's own teachers and students. When something does not work in a classroom, we find out the same week.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-gold btn-lg" href="mailto:mtcedarbritishinternationalsch@gmail.com?subject=ResultPeak%20%2F%20JDSmartLearn%20enquiry">Start a Conversation <span class="arr">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/portal">See the Portal</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
